THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE AND DATA
- None. OcuTrace is a single static page with no external libraries, fonts,
  or network requests. Video is processed in the browser and never uploaded.

NOTES
- The methods OcuTrace re-implements (dark-pupil/iris localization with
  centroid refinement, template matching for head-movement compensation,
  velocity-threshold detection of fast eye movements, slow phase velocity and
  square wave jerk measures, and the conversion from iris displacement to
  degrees of rotation) are published or standard methods in oculomotor
  research and are credited to their original authors. The MIT License covers
  OcuTrace's own source code and expression, not these underlying methods.
- OcuTrace is a research prototype. It is not a medical device, has not been
  cleared or approved by any regulator, and must not be used for diagnosis or
  treatment decisions.

